      "messageId": "user-msg-006a",
      "content": "We haven't really defined how ContextGraph should decide whether a piece of conversation is worth remembering at all. Before SAME or CHILD, there probably needs to be some gate that filters out things like thanks, random acknowledgments, and low-value conversational noise."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "messageId": "assistant-msg-006",
      "content": "So you're proposing a semantic significance layer before object decisions."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "messageId": "user-msg-006b",
      "content": "Exactly. And I think that's important enough to have its own rules because otherwise the graph will accumulate junk before the object algorithm even runs."
    }
